  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) Ice formed by heavy water sinks in normal water due to higher density of <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math> than normal water.<br /><br />(ii) <math> <mrow>  <mn>6</mn><msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>CO</mtext></mrow>   <mn>2</mn>  </msub>  <mo>+</mo><mtext>&#x2009;</mtext><mn>6</mn><msub>   <mtext>H</mtext>   <mn>2</mn>  </msub>  <mtext>O</mtext><munderover>   <mo>&#x2192;</mo>   <mrow>    <mtext>chlorophyll</mtext></mrow>   <mrow>    <mtext>hv</mtext></mrow>  </munderover>  <msub>   <mtext>C</mtext>   <mtext>6</mtext>  </msub>  <msub>   <mtext>H</mtext>   <mrow>    <mtext>12</mtext></mrow>  </msub>  <msub>   <mtext>O</mtext>   <mtext>6</mtext>  </msub>  <msub>   <mrow>    <mtext>+6O</mtext></mrow>   <mtext>2</mtext>  </msub>  </mrow></math><br /><br />(iii) Water can show amphiprotic nature and hence water can act both as an acid a base.<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/aqz.JPG\" style=\"width: 321px; height: 146px;\" /><br />(iv) There is extensive intermolecular hydrogen bonding in the condensed phase instead of intramolecular H - bonding.",
